#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to use stretch to defer timing resolution with dynamic circuits"
msgstr "Cómo usar stretch para diferir la resolución de temporización en circuitos dinámicos"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deferred timing resolution using stretch"
msgstr "Resolución de temporización diferida con stretch"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deferred timing resolution using stretch {#deferred-timing-resolution-using-stretch}"
msgstr "Resolución de temporización diferida con stretch {#deferred-timing-resolution-using-stretch}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The OpenQASM 3 language specification contains a `stretch` type with which you can specify relative timing of operations instead of absolute timing. Support for `stretch` as durations for [`Delay`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.Delay) instructions was added in [Qiskit v2.0.0](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/release-notes/2.0#200). The concrete value of a stretch duration is resolved at compile time, after the exact duration of calibrated gates are known.  The compiler tries to minimize the stretch duration, subject to timing constraints on one or more qubits. You can then express gate designs such as evenly spacing gates (for example, to implement a higher-order echo decoupling sequence), left-aligning a sequence of gates, or applying a gate for the duration of some sub-circuit, without knowing the exact timing.\n"
msgstr "La especificación del lenguaje OpenQASM 3 incluye un tipo `stretch` con el que puedes especificar la temporización relativa de las operaciones en lugar de la temporización absoluta. El soporte de `stretch` como duraciones para las instrucciones [`Delay`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.Delay) se añadió en [Qiskit v2.0.0](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/release-notes/2.0#200). El valor concreto de una duración stretch se resuelve en tiempo de compilación, una vez que se conocen las duraciones exactas de las puertas calibradas. El compilador intenta minimizar la duración del stretch, sujeto a las restricciones de temporización en uno o más qubits. Esto te permite expresar diseños de puertas como el espaciado uniforme de puertas (por ejemplo, para implementar una secuencia de desacoplamiento de eco de orden superior), la alineación izquierda de una secuencia de puertas, o la aplicación de una puerta durante la duración de algún subcircuito, sin necesidad de conocer la temporización exacta.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Examples {#examples}"
msgstr "Ejemplos {#examples}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamical decoupling {#dynamical-decoupling}"
msgstr "Desacoplamiento dinámico {#dynamical-decoupling}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A common use case of `stretch` is to apply dynamical decoupling to an idling qubit while another qubit is undergoing conditional operations.\n"
msgstr "Un caso de uso común de `stretch` es aplicar desacoplamiento dinámico a un qubit inactivo mientras otro qubit realiza operaciones condicionales.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, we can use `stretch` to apply an XX dynamical decoupling sequence to qubit 1, for the duration of the conditional block applied to qubit 0, as illustrated by the following diagram:\n"
msgstr "Por ejemplo, podemos usar `stretch` para aplicar una secuencia de desacoplamiento dinámico XX al qubit 1, durante la duración del bloque condicional aplicado al qubit 0, tal como se ilustra en el siguiente diagrama:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Image illustrating the following circuit](/docs/images/guides/stretch/stretch.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Imagen que ilustra el siguiente circuito](/docs/images/guides/stretch/stretch.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The corresponding circuit would look like the following. Note that a pair of barriers is needed to define the boundaries of this relative timing.\n"
msgstr "El circuito correspondiente tendría el siguiente aspecto. Ten en cuenta que se necesita un par de barreras para definir los límites de esta temporización relativa.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scheduling alignment {#scheduling-alignment}"
msgstr "Alineación de planificación {#scheduling-alignment}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example uses `stretch` to ensure a sequence of gates between two barriers are left-aligned, whatever their actual durations are:\n"
msgstr "Este ejemplo usa `stretch` para asegurar que una secuencia de puertas entre dos barreras quede alineada a la izquierda, independientemente de sus duraciones reales:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid " When using `stretch` with IBM Quantum Compute Service, any remainder resulting from a stretch resolution is added to the first delay that uses the stretch.\n"
msgstr " Al usar `stretch` con IBM Quantum Compute Service, cualquier resto resultante de una resolución de stretch se añade al primer delay que usa el stretch.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example:\n"
msgstr "Ejemplo:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"    circuit.barrier(q0, q1)\n"
"    circuit.delay(100, q0)\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 26\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 25\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 25\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.barrier(q0, q1)\n"
"     ```\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```python\n"
"    a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"    circuit.barrier(q0, q1)\n"
"    circuit.delay(100, q0)\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 26\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 25\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 25\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.barrier(q0, q1)\n"
"     ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The above code resolves to a value of 25 with a remainder of 1. The first delay`[a]` will have the remainder added.\n"
msgstr "El código anterior se resuelve con un valor de 25 y un resto de 1. El primer delay`[a]` tendrá el resto añadido.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stretch resolution equation:  $a + 8 + a + 8 + a + 8 = 100   =   3*a + 24$\n"
msgstr "Ecuación de resolución de stretch:  $a + 8 + a + 8 + a + 8 = 100   =   3*a + 24$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr "</DoqAdmonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "View stretch values in IBM Quantum Compute Service {#view-stretch-values-in-ibm-quantum-compute-service}"
msgstr "Ver los valores de stretch en IBM Quantum Compute Service {#view-stretch-values-in-ibm-quantum-compute-service}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The actual value of a stretch duration is resolved at compile time, after the circuit is scheduled. When running a Sampler job in IBM Quantum Compute Service, you can view the resolved stretch values in the job result metadata.  Support for `stretch` in Quantum Compute is currently experimental, so you need to first set an experimental option to enable its retrieval, then access the data directly from the metadata as follows:\n"
msgstr "El valor real de una duración stretch se resuelve en tiempo de compilación, después de que el circuito haya sido planificado. Al ejecutar un trabajo Sampler en IBM Quantum Compute Service, puedes ver los valores de stretch resueltos en los metadatos del resultado del trabajo. El soporte de `stretch` en Quantum Compute es actualmente experimental, por lo que primero debes establecer una opción experimental para habilitarlo, y luego acceder a los datos directamente desde los metadatos de la siguiente manera:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Although the total circuit time is returned in the \"compilation\" metadata, this is NOT the time used for billing (QPU time).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Aunque el tiempo total del circuito se devuelve en los metadatos de \"compilation\", este NO es el tiempo usado para la facturación (QPU time).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Understand the metadata output {#understand-the-metadata-output}"
msgstr "Entender la salida de metadatos {#understand-the-metadata-output}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `stretch_values` metadata returns the following information:\n"
msgstr "Los metadatos `stretch_values` devuelven la siguiente información:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Name:** The name of the applied stretch.\n"
msgstr "**Name:** El nombre del stretch aplicado.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Value:** The requested goal value.\n"
msgstr "**Value:** El valor objetivo solicitado.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Remainder:** The remainder from resolving the stretch, which is added to the first delay that uses the stretch.\n"
msgstr "**Remainder:** El resto de la resolución del stretch, que se añade al primer delay que usa el stretch.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Expanded values:** Sets of values that specify the stretch start and its duration.\n"
msgstr "**Expanded values:** Conjuntos de valores que especifican el inicio del stretch y su duración.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example {#example}"
msgstr "Ejemplo {#example}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Metadata output {#metadata-output}"
msgstr "Salida de metadatos {#metadata-output}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The values returned for duration depend on the goal value and the calculated remainder.  For example, these are the durations returned for foo:\n"
msgstr "Los valores devueltos para la duración dependen del valor objetivo y del resto calculado. Por ejemplo, estas son las duraciones devueltas para foo:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`foo value` + `remainder` (8+2 = 10) \n"
msgstr "`foo value` + `remainder` (8+2 = 10)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`foo value` * 3 (8 x 3 = 24)\n"
msgstr "`foo value` * 3 (8 x 3 = 24)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`foo value` * 2 (8 x 2 = 16)\n"
msgstr "`foo value` * 2 (8 x 2 = 16)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can use a visualization to help understand and verify the timing. \n"
msgstr "Puedes usar una visualización para ayudar a entender y verificar la temporización.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following image, based on the example output, `foo` corresponds to the stretches on Qubit 2. The first stretch delay that uses `foo` starts at the end of the `init_play` (1365). The stretch duration is 10, so that delay ends when the `x` gate starts (1365+10=1375). You can interpret the second and third stretches similarly.\n"
msgstr "En la siguiente imagen, basada en la salida del ejemplo, `foo` corresponde a los stretches en el Qubit 2. El primer stretch delay que usa `foo` comienza al final de `init_play` (1365). La duración del stretch es 10, por lo que ese delay termina cuando comienza la puerta `x` (1365+10=1375). Puedes interpretar el segundo y tercer stretches de manera similar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The output from the `draw_circuit_schedule_timing` command is shown.](/docs/images/guides/stretch/stretch-visualization.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Se muestra la salida del comando `draw_circuit_schedule_timing`.](/docs/images/guides/stretch/stretch-visualization.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the sliders at the bottom, the controls at the top (hover over your output image to reveal these), and the legend on the side of the output to customize the view. Hover over the image to view exact data.\n"
msgstr "Usa los controles deslizantes de la parte inferior, los controles de la parte superior (pasa el cursor sobre la imagen de salida para mostrarlos) y la leyenda del lateral para personalizar la vista. Pasa el cursor sobre la imagen para ver los datos exactos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For full details, see the [Visualize circuit timing](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing) topic.\n"
msgstr "Para obtener más detalles, consulta el tema [Visualizar la temporización del circuito](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qiskit-runtime-limitations\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum Compute limitations {#quantum-compute-limitations}"
msgstr "Limitaciones de Quantum Compute {#quantum-compute-limitations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Support for `stretch` in Quantum Compute is currently experimental and has the following constraints:\n"
msgstr "El soporte de `stretch` en Quantum Compute es actualmente experimental y tiene las siguientes restricciones:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- At most one stretch variable per _qubit set_ between barriers (implicit and explicit). A qubit set is one or more qubits; these sets must be mutually exclusive.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"Invalid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"- Como máximo una variable stretch por _conjunto de qubits_ entre barreras (implícitas y explícitas). Un conjunto de qubits es uno o más qubits; estos conjuntos deben ser mutuamente excluyentes.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"No válido\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, (q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(b, q0)  # Invalid because 2 stretches are applied on q0\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, (q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(b, q0)  # Invalid because 2 stretches are applied on q0\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Válido\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, (q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(b, q2)\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, (q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(b, q2)\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- The area surrounded by a set of barriers is called a _barrier region_. A stretch variable cannot be used in multiple barrier regions.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"Invalid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"- El área rodeada por un conjunto de barreras se denomina _región de barrera_. Una variable stretch no puede usarse en múltiples regiones de barrera.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"No válido\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        # Stretch a is used in two barrier regions\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"         ```\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        # Stretch a is used in two barrier regions\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"         ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "        ![Illustration of the previous code output](/docs/images/guides/stretch/bad-barrier-region.svg 'Invalid use of stretch in barrier regions')\n"
msgstr "        ![Ilustración de la salida del código anterior](/docs/images/guides/stretch/bad-barrier-region.svg 'Uso no válido de stretch en regiones de barrera')\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Válido\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        # Stretch a is used inside a barrier region that is on q0 and q1\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier(q2)\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        ```\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        # Stretch a is used inside a barrier region that is on q0 and q1\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier(q2)\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "        ![Illustration of the previous code output](/docs/images/guides/stretch/good-barrier-region.svg 'Valid use of stretch in a barrier region')\n"
msgstr "        ![Ilustración de la salida del código anterior](/docs/images/guides/stretch/good-barrier-region.svg 'Uso válido de stretch en una región de barrera')\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- Stretch expressions are limited to those of the form `X*stretch + Y` where `X` and `Y` are floating point or integer constants.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"Invalid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"- Las expresiones stretch están limitadas a las de la forma `X*stretch + Y` donde `X` e `Y` son constantes de punto flotante o enteras.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"No válido\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        c = circuit.add_stretch(\"c\")\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        c = circuit.add_stretch(\"c\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        # (a /  b) * c is not supported\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.mul(expr.div(a, b), c), q1)\n"
"         ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"        # (a /  b) * c is not supported\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.mul(expr.div(a, b), c), q1)\n"
"         ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Válido\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        from qiskit.circuit import Duration\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        from qiskit.circuit import Duration\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(expr.mul(a, 2), Duration.dt(3)), 0)\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(expr.mul(a, 2), Duration.dt(3)), 0)\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- Stretch expressions can only include a single stretch variable.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"        <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"Invalid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"- Las expresiones stretch solo pueden incluir una única variable stretch.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"        <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"No válido\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(a, b), 0)\n"
"         ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(a, b), 0)\n"
"         ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Válido\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(a, a), 0)\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(a, a), 0)\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    </Tabs>\n"
msgstr "    </Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- Stretch expressions cannot resolve to negative delay values. The current solver doesn't infer non-negativity constraints.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"Invalid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"- Las expresiones stretch no pueden resolverse a valores de delay negativos. El solucionador actual no infiere restricciones de no negatividad.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"No válido\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(20, q1)\n"
"        # The length of this barrier region is 20dt, meaning the\n"
"        # equation for solving stretch 'a' is a + 40dt = 20dt, giving a = -20dt.\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(a, Duration.dt(40)), q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"         ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(20, q1)\n"
"        # The length of this barrier region is 20dt, meaning the\n"
"        # equation for solving stretch 'a' is a + 40dt = 20dt, giving a = -20dt.\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(a, Duration.dt(40)), q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"         ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Válido\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(20, q1)\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(20, q1)\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
